{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts","id":546115,"title":"Hunter Kinship with Beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-08T17:10:25-07:00","id":546115,"title":"Hunter Kinship with Beasts","content":"So, upon reading the crossover potential for Hunter and Beast, it seems that the Beasts can form Kinship with those Hunters that have Endowments that come from their bloodline, like the Lucifuge and also they can do so with Slashers...<br /> Other Hunters can go on dream-quests and sacred hunts within the Primordial Dream to become kin to the Beasts too.<br /> <br /> So this thread is two-part, to talk about potential Kinships that some Hunters and Beasts could share (and the custom Nightmares formed once a 'Family Ties' Condition is enacted between a pair), also some discussion on how you would include Hunters delving into the Primordial Dream through a Beast's Primordial Pathway/Under the Bed mechanic or other method (such as messing with a graveyard's Avernian Gate when a cell are on patrol for monsters there perhaps). A Hunter who has the boost of dice that a Beast's <i>Mother's Kiss</i> can give and the possibly larger Resistance trait a Beast can offer the Hunter and +1 teamwork bonus through the '<i>Family Ties</i>' Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T23:48:03-07:00","id":546594,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd be a little more lenient- psychics and mediums (which are just muggles with supernatural merits after all) count, so why not vanguard? <br /> <br /> Anyway, the conspiracies can make for some interesting possible nightmares-<br /> <br /> Valkyrie- That's So Last Season: The target suddenly finds themselves confronted by a foe far better equipped then them.<br /> <br /> Promethean Brotherhood- Your Power is Mine: The target finds themselves without their magical powers, which are now turned against them.<br /> <br /> Vanguard- Your mind is an open book: The target finds the beast knows what they've done, what they're thinking, their mind and privacy violated.<br /> <br /> Faithful of Shulpae- Feast of Flesh, feast of Spirit: I'd think healing effects and satiety gains, I feel the fear here would be about being consumed alive for power, not the mimicry of abilities. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T00:57:58-07:00","id":546645,"title":"","content":"Ashford Abbey may have a custom Nightmare based around either impotence or everything becoming like gruel and tasteless. They're one of my favourite groups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:17:07-07:00","id":547132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=546594#post546594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I'd be a little more lenient- psychics and mediums (which are just muggles with supernatural merits after all) count, so why not vanguard?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>suspect</i> the rationale is being inherently different, and you always have been, even if you didn't know it. However, that seems to let out changelings. So personally I'd agree about things that make a deep-level change to you - VASCU's treatment, and the regimen the Ascending Ones have to do. Whether the magic using covenants come under that heading has mythos implications for the source and nature of their powers). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:53:10-07:00","id":547187,"title":"","content":"Well, with Changelings they are changed by Gentry and Arcadia, as much as a new Vampire is sired by an older one of their kind and a Sin-Eater just comes from someone the Geist happens to pick one day (though those who are gifted in seeing ghosts may be picked more). Humans can become wolf-blooded now (who can First Change to full Uratha) in 2e by being exposed to a strong case of Lunacy, not just through bloodline. Pretty much every other playable supernatural splat is when a normal person has something happen to them by something else doing something to them, outside of Mages possibly, also Demons (G-M ones, not Inferno ones) though it's explicitly stated that Demons are not related in any way shape or form to Beasts... Mages are also <i>only partially</i> related, a little less than the Vamps, Uratha and others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:05:37-07:00","id":547239,"title":"","content":"My personal theory is that VASCU isn't counted as Kin because the treatment they go through in order to develop their powers come from the God- Machine, but this is just because I claim that their Director Ops is an angel :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:32:22-07:00","id":547601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=547239#post547239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal theory is that VASCU isn't counted as Kin because the treatment they go through in order to develop their powers come from the God- Machine, but this is just because I claim that their Director Ops is an angel :P</div> </div> </div> </div>What would their Mission be, or are they an Exile? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:44:52-07:00","id":547943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=547239#post547239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal theory is that VASCU isn't counted as Kin because the treatment they go through in order to develop their powers come from the God- Machine, but this is just because I claim that their Director Ops is an angel :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Am I correct in recalling that Angels do not count as Kin, but the Unchained are officially adoptees?<br /> <br /> In contrast beings like the Gentry, Fetches, Pandorans, Stryx, the Hoast, etc etc would be as much &quot;kin&quot; as their related protagonist-types, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:01:48-07:00","id":547956,"title":"","content":"What about the Knights of St. George? While the Beasts may not like the name, their Goetic Gospels take advantage of a power from the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T21:52:56-07:00","id":547988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=547943#post547943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Am I correct in recalling that Angels do not count as Kin, but the Unchained are officially adoptees?<br /> <br /> In contrast beings like the Gentry, Fetches, Pandorans, Stryx, the Hoast, etc etc would be as much &quot;kin&quot; as their related protagonist-types, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are adoptees. The Unchained are considered in the same vain as that one dude at your family reunion who keeps showing up and drinking the punch and everyone passes him off a someone's husband/boyfriend but don't really know for sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T22:10:41-07:00","id":547993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=547988#post547988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prometheans are adoptees. The Unchained are considered in the same vain as that one dude at your family reunion who keeps showing up and drinking the punch and everyone passes him off a someone's husband/boyfriend but don't really know for sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not how I thought of them; the Unchained are more like a stranger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T23:41:44-07:00","id":548086,"title":"","content":"Angels and Demons are not Kin- they aren't even adopted. They are more like the co-workers who come to the family's dinner just to not offend their boss, but never feel quite comfortable in there.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I don't think there is any reason while the more.. scary.. monsters of WoD won't be considered part of the Family. Both Slashers and the strixs has been named as Family in the preview, if I'm not mistaken. Heck, some may be even more loved then the playable ones!<br /> <br /> @wander and about my VASCU theory- just think. Why would the God Machine need a gather a bunch of slashers all in one place? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:12:43-07:00","id":548147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=547132#post547132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>suspect</i> the rationale is being inherently different, and you always have been, even if you didn't know it. However, that seems to let out changelings. So personally I'd agree about things that make a deep-level change to you - VASCU's treatment, and the regimen the Ascending Ones have to do. Whether the magic using covenants come under that heading has mythos implications for the source and nature of their powers).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't really include the Ascending Ones, all they develop is a tolerance for poisons. The poison in the potions of AO aren't even part of the magic, it's something they add so that they won't abuse the potions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T00:22:07-07:00","id":552637,"title":"","content":"IDK about that, the Ascending Ones do have different regimes for their tolerance. I remember the original fiction for the AO is that the first made to use an Elixir had to &quot;purify&quot; himself. That could mean more than just a tolerance for Poison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:41:57-07:00","id":552738,"title":"","content":"The third actually. The first one used an unaltered potion and when it ran out after fighting non stop for over three years he died.<br /> <br /> The second one added poison to prevent that, and he dropped dead immediately from taking the poison.<br /> <br /> The third tempered the poison with prayer and self discipline, and he lived.<br /> <br /> So the elixirs work just fine without the poisons, and the fact that being subjected to mundane drugs and poisons helps with recreating an elixir suggests that the poison in elixirs is mundane.<br /> <br /> Sure the text says it's a matter of enlightenment, but the rules also say that there has never been an actual alchemist in AO, they just copy by rote (except for the adding poison part) formula by actual alchemists.<br /> <br /> How much enlightenment does rote copying really require?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T02:21:30-07:00","id":552767,"title":"","content":"turning their body into poison tolerate through self discipline and prayer sounds a lot like internal alchemy, and internal alchemy is also a type of alchemy.<br /> <br /> Also, they have a whole faction based around Hermetic Tradition and all other kinds of occult secrets, so I assume that at least some of them create new types of Elixirs, making them into alchemists in every sense of the word. Finally, even coping a rote used by an alchemist requires having at least some knowledge in alchemy, the same way the recreating a chemical experiment requires you to at least understand enough of chemistry to actually understand what to do and how it happen. Sure, you can just try to copy what has done before, but eventually you'll either understand some things about what you do or that you'll make a mistake- and in the case of the AO, mistake is more then likely to kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:33:47-07:00","id":553848,"title":"","content":"Yes, Compacts and Conspiracies talks about hermes the thrice great.<br /> <br /> It also discusses the djinn, one of the sources for new elixirs, rather than including rules for an AO to develop their own elixirs.<br /> <br /> If C&amp;C wanted to break the established rules of the setting and make AO actual alchemists than devoting word count on how to get elixirs out of djinn instead of providing rules on how to actually make your own elixirs is a really strange decision. <br /> <br /> Oh interesting little tidbit, I was reading book of the deceived and in one of the characters described themselves as a &quot;man of fire,&quot; so if one were so inclined one can make the djinn a connection between mummy and hunter.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, internal alchemy isn't a thing in egyptian alchemy, and if it was, then the AO suck at it, since it's only useful for tolerating poisons they put in their own elixirs. They can't even use it to tolerate other drugs or poisons. <br /> <br /> As for rote copying requiring knowledge of alchemy, not according to hunter. You didn't notice there's not a single dot of skill involved in making an elixir, it's made automatically, the only roll is to see how the body handles it, stamina plus elixir rating? Not a single dot in occult or science required. Which means an AO member could think the world is a flat and hollow riding on the back of a giant turtle and think Twilight is an accurate description of vampires as far as knowing anything about anything. <br /> <br /> They're not chefs, they're people slavishly following a cookbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:53:44-07:00","id":554354,"title":"","content":"I think that there is a rule for that- every time that the fluff and the mechanics contradict each other, fluff always win.<br /> <br /> The AO are presented as alchemists at every possible way, fluff wise- and you even have to admit that even if you just follow a cookbook, if you don't know how to cook your dish would still get out wrong- and for the AO, it usually means death. They need to learn alchemy if they like it or not.Even if they don't have the skills, mentally and fluff wise, they are alchemists. Even if internal alchemy is not the same as Egyptian alchemy, what they do sounds a lot like internal alchemy- and being specific to tolerate only their own poisons doesn't mean their body hasn't changed to simply support those poisons and nothing else. There are times when you need to judge something by the spirit, not the body of the things- and the AO are one such case. They are meant to be alchemists, and they are alchemists, and if the rules don't support it they should be changed.<br /> <br /> Also, there is an AO-Mummy connection. It is in Mortal Remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T01:53:33-07:00","id":555409,"title":"","content":"Except the fluff is that the AO are a cult, not alchemists. They are called a cult numerous times, how often are they called alchemists? In the core book, I believe that number is a big fat zero. So how can the fluff be that they're alchemists when they're never called such? <br /> <br /> The examples in the core book-<br /> <br /> An imam<br /> <br /> An accountant<br /> <br /> Bosnian refugee<br /> <br /> A drug dealer<br /> <br /> A junkie<br /> <br /> No chemists, no chemistry teachers, no biochemists, nothing. The closest thing to an occultist in the bunch is the accountant, who &quot;is an initiate of the seventh level,&quot; because he like the &quot;egyptian mysticism and drugs.&quot;<br /> <br /> The hermetic group you mentioned before, in C&amp;C it mentioned they have lots of members who don't even have elixir ratings, which means the group you suggests has the most alchemical knowledge has the most members who can't even use elixirs without dropping over dead. <br /> <br /> That makes it abundantly clear how little the AO actually have to do with alchemy. If you were correct, then the hermetics would be the masters of elixirs, not the reverse. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:31:56-07:00","id":556504,"title":"","content":"How I think Beasts might react to certain Compacts/Conspiracies:<br /> <br /> TFV: Too much like Heroes for my tastes.<br /> Malleus Malefacarium: See TFV.<br /> Ashwood Abbey: THEY DID <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><u><i><b>WHAT</b></i></u></span></span> TO MY SISTER!?!?!?!?!<br /> The Chiron Group: They steal body parts from my Family, so they can use them to hunt us? MOTHERFUCKERS!!<br /> The Lucifuge: Cousin!<br /> Null Mysterious: That's OK, we still believe in YOU.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:56:18-07:00","id":556799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=552738#post552738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure the text says it's a matter of enlightenment, but the rules also say that there has never been an actual alchemist in AO, they just copy by rote (except for the adding poison part) formula by actual alchemists.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's storyhooks in the Compact and Conspiracy about AO alchemists studying Prometheans for learning stuff, so I think the idea there's no actual alchemists is kinda silly. If there's fluff that says they're not actual alchemists, its contradicted by other fluff that does portray the group as having actual alchemists. <br /> <br /> I personally would consider AO to be distant Kin, but that's because I consider their brand of alchemy to be somehow related to Prometheans and the Principle, and we know that the Prommies are somehow related to the DM when the Unchained are not.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back on subject... I personally wouldn't allow VASCU or TFV to be considered Kin - they both sound a lot like things that the God Machine would have its hand in (I tend to run them as a join task force in play, so I tend to think of them as one Conspiracy with a choice of Endowments). And, even if TFV was not associated with the big GM, the fact is that they use magic equipment, not magic themselves. <br /> <br /> AKD can use relics based on their Supernal oath. At least, I think its supernal. So, I would actually consider them &quot;touched&quot; enough to qualify in some respects, but not benefit from the Mother's Kiss. Part of the AKD is the desire of some to become full mages again, while others hate the mages, so I think having a kind of slightly register would be good drama for both, but no other benefit to drive them both mad. So close, yet so far away. <br /> <br /> Lucifuge? It depends if we should be considering the Inferno to be Kin. I'm leaning to yes. Which is going to lead to some very interesting and pointed questions about the Dark Mother being a bad, bad girl.<br /> <br /> The Malleus Mailificorum? I'm not quite sure on them. It depends on the source of their magic. The obsession with vampires hints that we're talking about a link to LetS, which I consider to be GM powered. But Benedictions don't feel like something the GM or Principle would do, its definitely something dark behind it, while the angels and qashmal are more amoral. So I'm actually looking at something else. As a joke, I once said that Benedictions were powered by a particularly potent Mummy sealed in the Vatican vault for its tomb and treasures, and was manipulating the Catholics to try to take over the world, and saw vampires as the chief rival for shadow-control over the world. Other option was the Infernal again, or something else unnamed from the Lower Depths. In either case, having Beasts see the Witch Hammer as Kin would help emphasize that &quot;secretly dark source&quot; that Benediction seems to have, and so, I consider it to be appropriate here.<br /> <br /> TCG would register for each individual part. And likely horrify the Beasts. <br /> <br /> <br /> All other conspiracies are tied to appropriate supernaturals, and register partially as such, except, of course, the one with the angel tats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T20:09:24-07:00","id":577019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/546115-hunter-kinship-with-beasts?p=552767#post552767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Finally, even coping a rote used by an alchemist requires having at least some knowledge in alchemy, the same way the recreating a chemical experiment requires you to at least understand enough of chemistry to actually understand what to do and how it happen. Sure, you can just try to copy what has done before, but eventually you'll either understand some things about what you do or that you'll make a mistake- and in the case of the AO, mistake is more then likely to kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of Breaking Bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}